    "question": {
      ":question/id": "be14557b-ff69-53dc-a4c6-878e5298739f",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following systems is a first-order initial value problem?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $(2+x^2)\\left(\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}-2y\\right)+x{y}^{′}={e}^{x},\\,y(3)=-5,\\,{y}^{′}(3)=-4$\n- **II.** $(3+x^2)\\left(\\dfrac{dy}{dx}-2y\\right)+x{y}^{′}={e}^{x},\\,y(4)=3$\n- **III.** $(4+x^2)\\left(\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}-3y\\right)+x{y}^{′}={e}^{x},\\,y(3)=-3,\\,{y}^{′}(3)=-2$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "A first-order initial value problem (or IVP) is a first-order ordinary differential equation together with an initial condition that specifies a value of the unknown function at a point in its domain. A first-order initial value problem typically takes the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y({x}_{0})={y}_{0},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{0}$ and ${y}_{0}$ are constants.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each option.\n\n- System I is not a first-order initial value problem. It consists of a *second*-order differential equation $(2+x^2)\\left(\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}-2y\\right)+x{y}^{′}={e}^{x}$ together with *two* initial conditions $y(3)=-5,\\,{y}^{′}(3)=-4.$ This is a second-order initial value problem.\n\n- System II is a first-order initial value problem. It consists of a first-order differential equation $(3+x^2)\\left(\\dfrac{dy}{dx}-2y\\right)+x{y}^{′}={e}^{x}$ together with the initial condition $y(4)=3.$\n\n- System III is not a first-order initial value problem. It consists of a *second*-order differential equation $(4+x^2)\\left(\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}-3y\\right)+x{y}^{′}={e}^{x}$ together with *two* initial conditions $y(3)=-3,\\,{y}^{′}(3)=-2.$ This is a second-order initial value problem.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "c9acde03-185b-5d92-98d7-4eedc05247c3",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "37cfb44f-ec14-5f04-be99-74455e4e38f7",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
